# Next.js

- Respect the existing Next.js architecture unless there is a documented reason to change it.
- Keep server-only code server-side. Never import server secrets into Client Components.
- Do not expose privileged API operations through client-side code.
- Handle API errors explicitly.
- Do not blindly call `response.json()` when the response may not contain valid JSON.
- Handle empty responses, non-JSON responses, timeouts, and failed requests safely.

## AI translation

- AI translation must run through secure server-side code. Never expose an AI API key in browser/client code.
- Automatically translated content must support human review before publication.
- Handle API errors, timeouts, rate limits, retries, and invalid responses.
- Do not overwrite approved translations without explicit logic allowing it. Preserve the original source content.
